Package: hifiberry-tidal-connect
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         docker.io | docker-ce,
         docker-compose | docker-compose-plugin | docker-compose-v2
Recommends: hifiberry-audiocontrol (>= 0.6.18)
Description: Tidal Connect endpoint for HiFiBerry
 Turn a HiFiBerry into a Tidal Connect receiver: stream from the Tidal app on
 your phone directly to the attached HiFiBerry DAC.
 .
 The Tidal Connect binaries are proprietary 32-bit ARM executables that need
 legacy Debian Stretch libraries, so they run inside a Docker container built
 on the device at install time. Audio is routed to the host's PipeWire via the
 PulseAudio protocol.
XB-Hifiberry-Extension: yes
XB-Extension-Name: Tidal Connect
XB-Extension-Category: player
XB-Extension-Needs-Reboot: maybe
